	spec: "Invariant: a session that has nothing running never strands a message. (1) WAIT also ends when its own session holds a deliverable message: next-round or now messages from the human or other sessions, including ones that arrived before WAIT started. Queued (after-turn) messages move up to next-round, oldest first, keeping id and provenance, and stop at one being edited. Reports of its own background commands keep their normal delivery. Targets needing attention win over the message wake. (2) After a turn ends with <question>, queued and agent messages start turns like after any reply. The question stays open (notify.asked: attention notification, tab mark, WAIT attention) across those turns and restarts until a human text arrives that was not queued before, or for a delegated child a message from its parent, or a later text of the asking turn asks nothing. Marks keep it (turnMarks.asking). (3) A message to a turn parked on an approval question (any delivery; an agent's only while its tab is open) runs the turn: every held call of the batch gets a final result saying it did not run (the asked one: it waits for approval; the others: run again if needed), and the approval stays open beside the turn as a question of hidden /approve <call id> (turns.release), surviving restarts. Answering it runs the call once as a background Bash job, or declines it; the session hears either as a message from bash t<n>. A new approval or Escape dismisses it unrun. Requested by the user after 48-kim stayed in WAIT 48-let for 44 s while 48-let had already sent its reply (2026-11-17, session 48-lit); reviewed by gpt-6-astra.",
